        <skos:altLabel>Brainstem structure</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Brainstem structure (body structure)</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Three sections, the midbrain, pons and medulla oblongata, that are located at the base of the brain. The brain stem regulates the central nervous system, and is vital as a conduit for motor and sensory innervations. [NCIT]</skos:definition>
