        <skos:altLabel>Nebenniere</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>glandula suprarenalis</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A flattened, roughly triangular body resting upon the upper end of each kidney; it is one of the ductless glands furnishing internal secretions (epinephrine and norepinephrine from the medulla and steroid hormones from the cortex). [NCIT]</skos:definition>
        <skos:definition>A pair of glands located at the cranial pole of each of the two kidneys. Each adrenal gland is composed of two distinct endocrine tissues with separate embryonic origins, the adrenal cortex producing steroids and the adrenal medulla producing neurotransmitters. [MeSH]</skos:definition>
