        <skos:altLabel>Transitional zone of prostate</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>PI-RADS: Tissue around the urethra that is separated from the peripheral zone by the “surgical capsule” delineated as a low signal line on T2 weighted MRI.  It is the site of most BPH. [RADLEX]</skos:definition>
        <skos:definition>The region of the prostate gland that is located deep to both the central and peripheral zones; it surrounds the proximal urethra, and is the zone of the prostate gland that grows throughout life, most often causing a condition called benign prostatic hypertrophy. [NCIT]</skos:definition>
