        <rdfs:label>Lapatinib</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>GSK572016</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>GW 2016</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>GW2016</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>GW572016</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Lapatinib (substance)</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A synthetic, orally-active quinazoline with potential antineoplastic properties. Lapatinib reversibly blocks phosphorylation of the epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR), ErbB2, and the Erk-1 and-2 and AKT kinases; it also inhibits cyclin D protein levels in human tumor cell lines and xenografts. EGFR and ErbB2 have been implicated in the growth of various tumor types. [NCIT]</skos:definition>
        <skos:exactMatch>NCIT:C26653</skos:exactMatch>
        <skos:exactMatch>SNOMEDCT:425820005</skos:exactMatch>
        <skos:prefLabel>Lapatinib</skos:prefLabel>
