        <skos:altLabel>Magnetic resonance study</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>NMR - Nuclear magnetic resonance</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Imaging that uses radiofrequency waves and a strong magnetic field rather than x-rays to provide detailed pictures of internal organs and tissues. The technique is valuable for the diagnosis of many pathologic conditions, including cancer, heart and vascular disease, stroke, and joint and musculoskeletal disorders. [NCIT]</skos:definition>
        <skos:definition>Non-invasive method of demonstrating internal anatomy based on the principle that atomic nuclei in a strong magnetic field absorb pulses of radiofrequency energy and emit them as radiowaves which can be reconstructed into computerized images. The concept includes proton spin tomographic techniques. [MeSH]</skos:definition>
        <skos:exactMatch>NCIT:C16809</skos:exactMatch>
        <skos:exactMatch>RADLEX:RID10312</skos:exactMatch>
        <skos:exactMatch>UMLS:C0024485</skos:exactMatch>
